<answer> So, let $x=\sqrt{4+\sqrt{8+4c}}$, $y=\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}}$ with $x≥y$, we then notice that \begin{align} &  \sqrt{4+\sqrt{8+4c}}+ \sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}} = 2+2\sqrt{2} \\ \iff & \iff x+y=2+2\sqrt{2} \\ \iff & \iff x+2-y=2,\ \ \ \  x\geq y\\ \iff & \iff (x+2)^2+y^2-4xy=4,\ \ \ \ x\geq y\\ \iff & \iff (x^2-2\sqrt{2}x-4x+4)+(y^2-2\sqrt{2}y-4y+4)-4xy=0\\ \iff & \iff (x^2-2\sqrt{2}x+1-1-4x+4)+(y^2-2\sqrt{2}y+1-1-4y+4)-4xy=0\\ \iff & \iff \left(x-\sqrt{2}-1\right)^2+\left(y-\sqrt{2}-1\right)^2-4xy=0\\ \iff & \iff \left(x-\sqrt{2}-1\right)^2+\left(y-\sqrt{2}-1\right)^2-4\left(x-\sqrt{2}-1\right)(y-\sqrt{2}-1)=0\\ \iff & \iff \left(x-\sqrt{2}-1-\left(y-\sqrt{2}-1\right)\right)^2=0\\ \iff & \iff x=y+\sqrt{2} \geq 0\\ \iff & \iff \sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}}=c\geq 0\\ \implies & \iff 2c^2-4c-9+6\sqrt2=0\\ \iff & \iff 2c^2-4c+8+5\sqrt2=0\\ \iff & \iff c^2-2c+4+(5\sqrt2)/2=0\\ \iff & \iff \left(c-1\right)^2+4+(5\sqrt2)/2=0\\ \iff & \iff c=1+\sqrt{-\left(4+\frac{5\sqrt2}{2}\right)}*i\end{align}
 clearly $c≥0$, so we have no solution beyond that. Now, if $c≤0$, the LHS is no larger than  $2+2\sqrt{2}=RHS$ and we only have one solution i.e. $c=0$. </answer>

